    "subtitle": "Equazioni di primo grado",
    "text": "Risolvi le seguenti equazioni di primo grado:\n\\begin{multicols}{2}\n\\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=3cm]\n    \\item $4x + 1 = 2x + 9$\n    \\item $7 - 3x = x - 9$\n    \\item $2(3x - 1) + 4 = 5x + 7$\n    \\item $\\dfrac{2x+1}{3} = \\dfrac{x-2}{2}$\n\\end{enumerate}\n\\end{multicols}",
    "solution": "\\begin{enumerate}\n    \\item $x=4$\n    \\item $x=4$\n    \\item $x=5$\n    \\item $x=-8$\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "explanation": "\\begin{enumerate}\n    \\item \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    4x+1 &= 2x+9\\\\\n    4x-2x &= 9-1 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{$x$ a sinistra, numeri a destra}}\\\\\n    2x &= 8\\\\\n    x &= 4 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{divido per $2$}}\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    \\item \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    7-3x &= x-9\\\\\n    -3x-x &= -9-7\\\\\n    -4x &= -16\\\\\n    x &= 4 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{divido per $-4$}}\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    \\item \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    2(3x-1)+4 &= 5x+7\\\\\n    6x-2+4 &= 5x+7 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{svolgo la parentesi}}\\\\\n    6x-5x &= 7-2\\\\\n    x &= 5\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    \\item \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    \\dfrac{2x+1}{3} &= \\dfrac{x-2}{2}\\\\\n    2(2x+1) &= 3(x-2) && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{moltiplico per il m.c.m. $6$}}\\\\\n    4x+2 &= 3x-6\\\\\n    4x-3x &= -6-2\\\\\n    x &= -8\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "id": 225
