    "subtitle": "Sistemi lineari con parentesi e frazioni",
    "text": "Risolvi i seguenti sistemi lineari di due equazioni:\r\n\\begin{multicols}{2}\r\n\\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=3.2cm]\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    2(x+y)=10\\\\\r\n    3x-y=5\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    \\dfrac{x}{2}+\\dfrac{y}{3}=3\\\\\r\n    x-y=1\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    3(x-1)+2y=7\\\\\r\n    x+y=3\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    \\dfrac{2x-1}{3}+y=4\\\\\r\n    x-\\dfrac{y+1}{2}=2\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\\end{enumerate}\r\n\\end{multicols}",
    "solution": "\\begin{enumerate}\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=\\left(\\tfrac52,\\tfrac52\\right)$\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=(4,3)$\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=(4,-1)$\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=\\left(\\tfrac72,2\\right)$\r\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "explanation": "Prima si porta ogni equazione nella \\textbf{forma normale} $ax+by=c$ (svolgendo le parentesi ed eliminando i denominatori), poi si risolve.\r\n\\begin{enumerate}\r\n    \\item Divido la prima equazione per $2$: diventa $x+y=5$. La $y$ ha coefficienti opposti nelle due equazioni: sommo.\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    (x+y)+(3x-y) &= 5+5\\\\\r\n    4x &= 10\\\\\r\n    x &= \\dfrac52\\\\\r\n    y &= 5-\\dfrac52=\\dfrac52 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{da $x+y=5$}}\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n    \\item Moltiplico la prima per il m.c.m. $6$: $3x+2y=18$. Dalla seconda: $x=y+1$.\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    3(y+1)+2y &= 18 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{sostituisco}}\\\\\r\n    5y+3 &= 18\\\\\r\n    y &= 3\\\\\r\n    x &= 4\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n    \\item Prima equazione: $3x-3+2y=7$, cioè $3x+2y=10$. Dalla seconda: $x=3-y$.\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    3(3-y)+2y &= 10 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{sostituisco}}\\\\\r\n    9-y &= 10\\\\\r\n    y &= -1\\\\\r\n    x &= 3-(-1)=4\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n    \\item Elimino i denominatori:\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    2x-1+3y &= 12 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{prima equazione per $3$}}\\\\\r\n    2x+3y &= 13\\\\\r\n    2x-(y+1) &= 4 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{seconda equazione per $2$}}\\\\\r\n    2x-y &= 5\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n    La $x$ ha lo stesso coefficiente: sottraggo la seconda dalla prima.\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    (2x+3y)-(2x-y) &= 13-5\\\\\r\n    4y &= 8\\\\\r\n    y &= 2\\\\\r\n    2x &= 5+2 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; x=\\dfrac72 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{da $2x-y=5$}}\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "id": 270
