    "text": "Risolvi i seguenti sistemi lineari di due equazioni:\r\n\\begin{multicols}{2}\r\n\\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=3.2cm]\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    4x-3y=1\\\\\r\n    5x+2y=19\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    \\dfrac{3x+y}{2}=5\\\\\r\n    \\dfrac{x-y}{3}=1\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    2(x-2)-3(y+1)=4\\\\\r\n    5x+2y=13\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    \\dfrac{2x-3y}{4}=2\\\\\r\n    \\dfrac{x+y}{3}=2\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\\end{enumerate}\r\n\\end{multicols}",
    "solution": "\\begin{enumerate}\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=\\left(\\tfrac{59}{23},\\tfrac{71}{23}\\right)$\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=\\left(\\tfrac{13}{4},\\tfrac14\\right)$\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=\\left(\\tfrac{61}{19},-\\tfrac{29}{19}\\right)$\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=\\left(\\tfrac{26}{5},\\tfrac45\\right)$\r\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "explanation": "\\begin{enumerate}\r\n    \\item Nessun coefficiente vale $1$: uso la riduzione. Per eliminare la $y$ rendo i suoi coefficienti opposti ($-6y$ e $+6y$):\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    8x-6y &= 2 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{prima equazione per $2$}}\\\\\r\n    15x+6y &= 57 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{seconda equazione per $3$}}\\\\\r\n    23x &= 59 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{sommo}}\\\\\r\n    x &= \\dfrac{59}{23}\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n    Ricavo $y$ dalla prima equazione, $3y=4x-1$:\r\n    \\[ 3y=\\dfrac{236}{23}-\\dfrac{23}{23}=\\dfrac{213}{23} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; y=\\dfrac{71}{23} \\]\r\n    \\item Elimino i denominatori: $3x+y=10$ (per $2$) e $x-y=3$ (per $3$). La $y$ ha coefficienti opposti: sommo.\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    4x &= 13\\\\\r\n    x &= \\dfrac{13}{4}\\\\\r\n    y &= x-3=\\dfrac{13}{4}-\\dfrac{12}{4}=\\dfrac14\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n    \\item Prima equazione in forma normale: $2x-4-3y-3=4$, cioè $2x-3y=11$. Riduzione sulla $y$:\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    4x-6y &= 22 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{prima per $2$}}\\\\\r\n    15x+6y &= 39 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{seconda per $3$}}\\\\\r\n    19x &= 61 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{sommo}}\\\\\r\n    x &= \\dfrac{61}{19}\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n    Da $3y=2x-11$: \\ $3y=\\tfrac{122}{19}-\\tfrac{209}{19}=-\\tfrac{87}{19} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; y=-\\tfrac{29}{19}$.\r\n    \\item Elimino i denominatori: $2x-3y=8$ (per $4$) e $x+y=6$ (per $3$). Dalla seconda: $x=6-y$.\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    2(6-y)-3y &= 8 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{sostituisco}}\\\\\r\n    12-5y &= 8\\\\\r\n    y &= \\dfrac45\\\\\r\n    x &= 6-\\dfrac45=\\dfrac{26}{5}\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "id": 271
