    "text": "Risolvi i seguenti sistemi lineari di due equazioni:\r\n\\begin{multicols}{2}\r\n\\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=3.2cm]\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    \\dfrac{1}{2}x+\\dfrac{1}{3}y=3\\\\\r\n    x-y=1\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    \\dfrac{1}{3}x+\\dfrac{1}{2}y=3\\\\\r\n    2x-y=2\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    \\dfrac{1}{4}x+y=4\\\\\r\n    \\dfrac{1}{2}x-\\dfrac{1}{3}y=1\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    \\dfrac{1}{2}x+\\dfrac{1}{5}y=4\\\\\r\n    x-\\dfrac{1}{2}y=-1\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\\end{enumerate}\r\n\\end{multicols}",
    "solution": "\\begin{enumerate}\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=(4,3)$\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=(3,4)$\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=(4,3)$\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=(4,10)$\r\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "explanation": "Si moltiplica ogni equazione per il m.c.m. dei suoi denominatori, così i coefficienti diventano interi; poi si risolve per sostituzione o riduzione.\r\n\\begin{enumerate}\r\n    \\item Prima equazione per $6$: $3x+2y=18$. Dalla seconda: $x=y+1$.\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    3(y+1)+2y &= 18 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{sostituisco}}\\\\\r\n    5y &= 15\\\\\r\n    y &= 3, \\qquad x=4\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n    \\item Prima equazione per $6$: $2x+3y=18$. Dalla seconda: $y=2x-2$.\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    2x+3(2x-2) &= 18 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{sostituisco}}\\\\\r\n    8x-6 &= 18\\\\\r\n    x &= 3, \\qquad y=4\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n    \\item Prima per $4$: $x+4y=16$; \\ seconda per $6$: $3x-2y=6$. Dalla prima: $x=16-4y$.\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    3(16-4y)-2y &= 6 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{sostituisco}}\\\\\r\n    48-14y &= 6\\\\\r\n    y &= 3, \\qquad x=16-12=4\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n    \\item Prima per $10$: $5x+2y=40$; \\ seconda per $2$: $2x-y=-2$, da cui $y=2x+2$.\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    5x+2(2x+2) &= 40 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{sostituisco}}\\\\\r\n    9x+4 &= 40\\\\\r\n    x &= 4, \\qquad y=10\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "id": 273
