    "text": "Risolvi i seguenti sistemi lineari di due equazioni:\r\n\\begin{multicols}{2}\r\n\\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=3.2cm]\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    \\dfrac{x+1}{2}+\\dfrac{1}{3}y=3\\\\\r\n    x-\\dfrac{1}{3}y=2\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    \\dfrac{1}{4}x+\\dfrac{y-1}{3}=2\\\\\r\n    x-\\dfrac{1}{2}y=2\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    \\dfrac{x-2}{3}+\\dfrac{1}{2}y=3\\\\\r\n    2x-y=6\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\r\n    \\item\r\n    \\[\r\n    \\begin{cases}\r\n    \\dfrac{1}{2}x+\\dfrac{y+1}{4}=3\\\\\r\n    \\dfrac{x-1}{3}+y=4\r\n    \\end{cases}\r\n    \\]\r\n\\end{enumerate}\r\n\\end{multicols}",
    "solution": "\\begin{enumerate}\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=(3,3)$\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=(4,4)$\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=(5,4)$\r\n    \\item $(x,y)=(4,3)$\r\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "explanation": "\\begin{enumerate}\r\n    \\item Elimino i denominatori:\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    3(x+1)+2y &= 18 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; 3x+2y=15 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{prima per $6$}}\\\\\r\n    3x-y &= 6 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{seconda per $3$}}\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n    La $x$ ha lo stesso coefficiente: sottraggo la seconda dalla prima.\r\n    \\[ 3y=9 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; y=3, \\qquad 3x=6+3 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; x=3 \\]\r\n    \\item Prima per $12$: $3x+4(y-1)=24$, cioè $3x+4y=28$; \\ seconda per $2$: $2x-y=4$, da cui $y=2x-4$.\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    3x+4(2x-4) &= 28 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{sostituisco}}\\\\\r\n    11x-16 &= 28\\\\\r\n    x &= 4, \\qquad y=4\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n    \\item Prima per $6$: $2(x-2)+3y=18$, cioè $2x+3y=22$; \\ dalla seconda $y=2x-6$.\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    2x+3(2x-6) &= 22\\\\\r\n    8x &= 40\\\\\r\n    x &= 5, \\qquad y=4\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n    \\item Prima per $4$: $2x+y+1=12$, cioè $2x+y=11$; \\ seconda per $3$: $x-1+3y=12$, cioè $x+3y=13$. \\\\\r\n    Dalla prima $y=11-2x$:\r\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\r\n    x+3(11-2x) &= 13\\\\\r\n    -5x+33 &= 13\\\\\r\n    x &= 4, \\qquad y=3\r\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\r\n\\end{enumerate}",
