    "solution": "\\begin{enumerate}[label=\\arabic*)]\n    \\item $y=x$; \\ interseca l'asse $y$ in $(0,0)$\n    \\item $y=-\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\left(x-\\tfrac{\\pi}{3}\\right)+\\tfrac12$; \\ interseca l'asse $y$ in $\\left(0,\\ \\tfrac12+\\tfrac{\\sqrt3\\,\\pi}{6}\\right)\\approx(0;\\ 1{,}41)$\n    \\item $y=\\tfrac14(x-2)+2$; \\ interseca l'asse $y$ in $\\left(0,\\tfrac32\\right)$\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "explanation": "Uso $y=f(x_0)+f'(x_0)(x-x_0)$. Una retta non verticale interseca sempre l'asse $y$: il punto si trova ponendo $x=0$.\n\\begin{enumerate}[label=\\arabic*)]\n    \\item \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    f(1) &= 1-2+2=1\\\\\n    f'(x) &= 3x^2-2 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; f'(1)=1\\\\\n    y &= 1+1\\cdot(x-1)=x\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    Per $x=0$: $y=0$. La tangente passa per l'origine.\n    \\item \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    f\\left(\\dfrac\\pi3\\right) &= \\cos\\dfrac\\pi3=\\dfrac12\\\\\n    f'(x) &= -\\sin x \\;\\Rightarrow\\; f'\\left(\\dfrac\\pi3\\right)=-\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\\n    y &= \\dfrac12-\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\left(x-\\dfrac\\pi3\\right)\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    Per $x=0$: $y=\\tfrac12+\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\cdot\\tfrac\\pi3=\\tfrac12+\\tfrac{\\sqrt3\\,\\pi}{6}\\approx1{,}41$.\n    \\item \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    f(2) &= \\sqrt4=2\\\\\n    f'(x) &= \\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; f'(2)=\\dfrac14\\\\\n    y &= 2+\\dfrac14(x-2)\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    Per $x=0$: $y=2-\\tfrac12=\\tfrac32$.\n\\end{enumerate}",
