    "text": "Risolvi i seguenti integrali indefiniti\n\n\\begin{center}\\begin{minipage}{0.7\\linewidth}\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item $\\int (2x^3 - x^2 + 4x -1) \\ dx$\n\\item $\\int \\frac{2x+1}{x^2+x} \\ dx$\n\\item $\\int \\frac{1}{x \\cdot \\ln x} \\ dx$\n\\item $\\int \\sqrt{16- x^2} \\ dx$\n\\item $\\int x \\cdot e^{x} \\ dx$\n\\item $\\int \\frac{dx}{\\cos^2(3x)}$\n\\item $\\int \\frac{1}{x^2 + 2x + 10} \\ dx$\n\\item $\\int \\frac{2x+1}{x^2-9} \\ dx$\n\\end{enumerate}\n\\end{minipage}\\end{center}",
    "solution": "\\begin{enumerate}\n    \\item $\\tfrac12x^4-\\tfrac13x^3+2x^2-x+C$\n    \\item $\\ln|x^2+x|+C$\n    \\item $\\ln|\\ln x|+C$\n    \\item $\\tfrac x2\\sqrt{16-x^2}+8\\arcsin\\tfrac x4+C$\n    \\item $e^x(x-1)+C$\n    \\item $\\tfrac13\\tan(3x)+C$\n    \\item $\\tfrac13\\arctan\\tfrac{x+1}{3}+C$\n    \\item $\\tfrac76\\ln|x-3|+\\tfrac56\\ln|x+3|+C$\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "explanation": "\\begin{enumerate}\n    \\item Termine per termine: \\ $2\\cdot\\dfrac{x^4}{4}-\\dfrac{x^3}{3}+4\\cdot\\dfrac{x^2}{2}-x+C=\\dfrac12x^4-\\dfrac13x^3+2x^2-x+C$.\n    \\item Il numeratore $2x+1$ è esattamente la derivata del denominatore $x^2+x$:\n    \\[ \\int\\dfrac{f'(x)}{f(x)}\\,dx=\\ln|f(x)|+C \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\ln|x^2+x|+C \\]\n    \\item $\\dfrac1x$ è la derivata di $\\ln x$: l'integrale ha la forma $\\int\\dfrac{t'}{t}\\,dx$ con $t=\\ln x$.\n    \\[ \\int\\dfrac{1/x}{\\ln x}\\,dx=\\ln|\\ln x|+C \\]\n    \\item Come per $\\sqrt{9-x^2}$, con la sostituzione $x=4\\sin t$:\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    \\int\\sqrt{16-x^2}\\,dx &= \\int16\\cos^2t\\,dt=8(t+\\sin t\\cos t)+C\\\\\n    &= 8\\arcsin\\dfrac x4+\\dfrac x2\\sqrt{16-x^2}+C\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    \\item Per parti con $f=x$ e $g'=e^x$:\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    \\int xe^x\\,dx &= xe^x-\\int e^x\\,dx\\\\\n    &= xe^x-e^x+C=e^x(x-1)+C\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    \\item $\\dfrac{1}{\\cos^2t}$ è la derivata di $\\tan t$; con $t=3x$ serve il fattore $3$:\n    \\[ \\int\\dfrac{dx}{\\cos^2(3x)}=\\dfrac13\\int\\dfrac{3}{\\cos^2(3x)}\\,dx=\\dfrac13\\tan(3x)+C \\]\n    \\item Completo il quadrato: $x^2+2x+10=(x+1)^2+9$, poi uso $\\int\\dfrac{dt}{t^2+a^2}=\\dfrac1a\\arctan\\dfrac ta$ con $a=3$:\n    \\[ \\dfrac13\\arctan\\dfrac{x+1}{3}+C \\]\n    \\item $x^2-9=(x-3)(x+3)$: fratti semplici.\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    2x+1 &= A(x+3)+B(x-3)\\\\\n    x=3:\\ 7 &= 6A \\;\\Rightarrow\\; A=\\dfrac76\\\\\n    x=-3:\\ -5 &= -6B \\;\\Rightarrow\\; B=\\dfrac56\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    Quindi $\\tfrac76\\ln|x-3|+\\tfrac56\\ln|x+3|+C$ \\ (equivale a $\\ln|x^2-9|+\\tfrac16\\ln\\left|\\tfrac{x-3}{x+3}\\right|+C$).\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "id": 340
