    "text": "Risolvi le seguenti equazioni esponenziali:\n\\begin{center}\\begin{minipage}{0.92\\linewidth}\n\\begin{multicols}{2}\n\\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=3.2cm]\n\\item $\\sqrt{8^{x}} = 4^{x-1}$\n\\item $3^{x+1} + 3^{x} = 36$\n\\item $5^{x+1} - 5^{x} + 5^{x-1} = 105$\n\\item $\\dfrac{\\sqrt[3]{2^{x-1}}}{\\sqrt{4^{x+1}}} = \\sqrt{8}$\n\\end{enumerate}\n\\end{multicols}\n\\end{minipage}\\end{center}",
    "solution": "\\begin{enumerate}\n    \\item $x=4$\n    \\item $x=2$\n    \\item $x=2$\n    \\item $x=-\\tfrac{17}{4}$\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "explanation": "\\textbf{Stessa base}: si scrivono i due membri come potenze della stessa base; poiché l'esponenziale è iniettiva, $a^{f(x)}=a^{g(x)} \\iff f(x)=g(x)$.\n\\begin{enumerate}\n    \\item \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    (2^{3x})^{1/2} &= 2^{2(x-1)}\\\\\n    \\dfrac32x &= 2x-2 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; x=4\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    \\item Raccolgo la potenza con l'esponente più basso, $3^x$:\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    3^x(3+1) &= 36\\\\\n    3^x &= 9 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; x=2\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    \\item Raccolgo $5^{x-1}$:\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    5^{x-1}(5^2-5+1) &= 105\\\\\n    21\\cdot5^{x-1} &= 105 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; 5^{x-1}=5 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; x=2\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    \\item \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    \\dfrac{2^{(x-1)/3}}{2^{x+1}} &= 2^{3/2} && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{$\\sqrt{4^{x+1}}=2^{x+1}$, \\ $\\sqrt8=2^{3/2}$}}\\\\\n    \\dfrac{x-1}{3}-(x+1) &= \\dfrac32\\\\\n    2x-2-6x-6 &= 9 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{moltiplico per $6$}}\\\\\n    x &= -\\dfrac{17}{4}\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "id": 537
