    "explanation": "\\textbf{Incognita ausiliaria}: si pone $t=a^x$ (con $t>0$), si risolve l'equazione in $t$, si scartano le soluzioni $t\\leq0$ e si torna alla $x$.\n\\begin{enumerate}\n    \\item $3^{2-x}=\\dfrac{9}{3^x}$; con $t=3^x$:\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    t+\\dfrac9t &= 10\\\\\n    t^2-10t+9 &= 0 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{moltiplico per $t>0$}}\\\\\n    t=1,\\ t=9 &\\;\\Rightarrow\\; x=0,\\ x=2\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    \\item $\\left(\\tfrac32\\right)^x=\\dfrac1t$ con $t=\\left(\\tfrac23\\right)^x$:\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    t+\\dfrac1t &= \\dfrac{97}{36}\\\\\n    36t^2-97t+36 &= 0\\\\\n    t &= \\dfrac{97\\pm\\sqrt{9409-5184}}{72}=\\dfrac{97\\pm65}{72} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; t=\\dfrac94,\\ t=\\dfrac49\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    $\\left(\\tfrac23\\right)^x=\\tfrac49=\\left(\\tfrac23\\right)^2 \\Rightarrow x=2$; \\ $\\left(\\tfrac23\\right)^x=\\tfrac94=\\left(\\tfrac23\\right)^{-2} \\Rightarrow x=-2$.\n    \\item $t=2^x$: $8^x=t^3$, $4^x=t^2$.\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    t^3-6t^2+8t &= 0\\\\\n    t(t-2)(t-4) &= 0\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    $t=0$ non accettabile; $t=2 \\Rightarrow x=1$; $t=4 \\Rightarrow x=2$.\n    \\item $t=2^x$: \\ $2^{x+2}=4t$, \\ $2^{x+1/2}=\\sqrt2\\,t$.\n    \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    t^2-4t-\\sqrt2\\,t+4\\sqrt2 &= 0\\\\\n    t(t-4)-\\sqrt2(t-4) &= 0 && \\textcolor{gray}{\\text{raccoglimento parziale}}\\\\\n    (t-4)(t-\\sqrt2) &= 0\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    $2^x=4 \\Rightarrow x=2$; \\ $2^x=\\sqrt2=2^{1/2} \\Rightarrow x=\\tfrac12$.\n\\end{enumerate}",
