    "subtitle": "Equazioni goniometriche con duplicazione — serie 4",
    "text": "Risolvi le seguenti equazioni:\n\\begin{multicols}{2}\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item $\\sin 2x = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\n\\item $\\cos(3x + \\pi/6) = \\dfrac{1}{2}$\n\\item $\\tan(x - \\pi/3) = -\\sqrt{3}$\n\\item $2 \\cos^2 x - 1 = 0$\n\\item $\\sin x \\cos x = \\dfrac{1}{4}$\n\\item $\\sin x - \\cos x = 0$\n\\end{enumerate}\n\\end{multicols}",
    "solution": "\\begin{enumerate}\n    \\item $x=\\tfrac\\pi6+k\\pi \\vee x=\\tfrac\\pi3+k\\pi$\n    \\item $x=\\tfrac\\pi{18}+\\tfrac23k\\pi \\vee x=-\\tfrac\\pi6+\\tfrac23k\\pi$\n    \\item $x=k\\pi$\n    \\item $x=\\tfrac\\pi4+k\\tfrac\\pi2$\n    \\item $x=\\tfrac\\pi{12}+k\\pi \\vee x=\\tfrac5{12}\\pi+k\\pi$\n    \\item $x=\\tfrac\\pi4+k\\pi$\n\\end{enumerate}",
    "explanation": "Soluzioni con $k\\in\\mathbb{Z}$. Equazioni elementari: \\ $\\sin\\theta=s \\Rightarrow \\theta=\\theta_0+2k\\pi \\vee \\theta=\\pi-\\theta_0+2k\\pi$; \\ $\\cos\\theta=c \\Rightarrow \\theta=\\pm\\theta_0+2k\\pi$; \\ $\\tan\\theta=t \\Rightarrow \\theta=\\theta_0+k\\pi$. Se l'argomento è un'espressione $\\theta=ax+b$, si risolve prima in $\\theta$ e poi si ricava $x$ (dividendo anche il periodo per $a$).\n\\begin{enumerate}\n    \\item $2x=\\tfrac\\pi3+2k\\pi \\vee 2x=\\tfrac23\\pi+2k\\pi$, poi divido per $2$.\n    \\item \\[\\begin{aligned}\n    3x+\\dfrac\\pi6 &= \\dfrac\\pi3+2k\\pi \\;\\Rightarrow\\; 3x=\\dfrac\\pi6+2k\\pi \\;\\Rightarrow\\; x=\\dfrac\\pi{18}+\\dfrac23k\\pi\\\\\n    3x+\\dfrac\\pi6 &= -\\dfrac\\pi3+2k\\pi \\;\\Rightarrow\\; 3x=-\\dfrac\\pi2+2k\\pi \\;\\Rightarrow\\; x=-\\dfrac\\pi6+\\dfrac23k\\pi\n    \\end{aligned}\\]\n    \\item $x-\\tfrac\\pi3=-\\tfrac\\pi3+k\\pi \\Rightarrow x=k\\pi$.\n    \\item Duplicazione: $2\\cos^2x-1=\\cos2x=0 \\Rightarrow 2x=\\tfrac\\pi2+k\\pi \\Rightarrow x=\\tfrac\\pi4+k\\tfrac\\pi2$.\n    \\item $\\sin x\\cos x=\\tfrac12\\sin2x$, quindi $\\sin2x=\\tfrac12$: come in 4.2 a).\n    \\item $\\cos x=0$ non è soluzione; divido: $\\tan x=1 \\Rightarrow x=\\tfrac\\pi4+k\\pi$.\n\\end{enumerate}",
